				</svg></button></div></form></div></div></header><div class="site-inner" id="main-content"><div class="content-area"><main class="site-main" role="main"><article class="type-post"><div class="entry-content"><div class="post-header"><p id="breadcrumbs" class="breadcrumb"><span><span><a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/">Home</a></span> <span class="sep">›</span> <span><a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/category/bubble-tea/">Bubble Teas</a></span></span></p><h1 class="entry-title">Classic Bubble Tea Recipe</h1><div class="post-header__info"><div><p class="entry-author">By <a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/about/">Jee Choe</a></p><p class="post-date">on  Apr 16, 2025</p></div></div><div><div class="aff-disc"><p>This post may contain affiliate links. As an Amazon Associate, I earn from qualifying purchases.</p>
</div></div></div><div class="post-intro"><div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex"><a href="https://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url=https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/how-to-make-bubble-tea/&amp;media=https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/pin-boba-milk-tea-1.jpg&amp;description=Classic Bubble Tea Recipe" title="Share on Pinterest"  target="_blank"  rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"  class="wp-element-button" data-postid="27035" data-pin-do="none" data-social-network="Pinterest" data-social-action="Pin" data-social-target="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/how-to-make-bubble-tea/"><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" role="img" focusable="false"><use href="#utility-pinterest-alt"></use></svg>Pin this Recipe</a><a class="wp-element-button" href="#wprm-recipe-container-27236"><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" role="img" focusable="false"><use href="#utility-chevron-down"></use></svg>Jump to Recipe</a></div></div><!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/loose.dtd">
<p>Bubble tea goes by many names, including boba, milk tea, and boba milk tea. See how easy it is to make boba at home and get my tips to making it delicious.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-11.jpg" alt="Bubble Tea, or Boba Milk Tea, in a clear glass with a wide, black straw.
" class="wp-image-27046" srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-11.jpg 1200w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-11-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-11-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-11-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-11-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-11-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></figure><br><div class="block-email cwp-large has-background has-quaternary-background-color">
