<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="bubble-tea">Bubble Tea</h2>



<p>Bubble tea is a cold drink usually made with tea, sugar, ice, and tapioca balls. Originally from Taiwan, boba was created in the 1980s. Bubble tea is also called boba, milk tea, and boba milk tea. </p>



<p>Tapioca balls, or <strong><a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/boba/">boba,</a></strong> are the &ldquo;bubbles&rdquo; in bubble tea. Tapioca balls are made from tapioca starch from the cassava root. Normally, tapioca is white, not black, but the black color in tapioca balls comes from brown sugar or caramel coloring added to the cassava. This makes the boba sweeter than it would be otherwise.</p>



<p>A wide straw is served with boba is so you can enjoy some tapioca balls with each sip of the tea. </p>



<p><strong>RELATED: <a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/brown-sugar-milk-tea/">Brown Sugar Bubble Tea</a></strong></p>


<div class="block-tip cwp-inner block-tip--has-image">

<h2 class="wp-block-heading block-tip__title" id="note-from-jee">Note from Jee</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image alignright size-full is-resized is-style-rounded"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="" class="wp-image-41994" style="width:200px" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a.jpg 1200w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-400x400.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-500x500.jpg 500w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-300x300.jpg 300w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1200" src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-41994" style="width:200px" srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a.jpg 1200w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-400x400.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-500x500.jpg 500w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/profile-2024-3a-300x300.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<p>When I first made bubble tea at home, I was surprised at how easy it was. </p>



<p>The tea part of bubble tea is just tea with milk and sugar. The bubble part of bubble tea is tapioca balls. I get store-bought, vacuum-sealed, dried tapioca balls and cook them in water to plump them up. Most of the recipe is just boiling water!</p>

</div>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="recipe-summary">Recipe Summary</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>A classic boba recipe made easy with store-bought tapioca balls and black tea. </li>



<li>A lot of bubble tea shops use powdered tea and powdered milk but this homemade recipe uses real brewed tea and any milk of your choice.</li>



<li>The brown sugar in the drink gives it a deeper, richer flavor than regular sugar since it has notes of molasses and toffee.</li>



<li>My tried-and-true secret to making the best bubble tea is to use very warm tapioca balls. That perfectly soft and chewy texture of boba you&rsquo;re looking for is there when they&rsquo;re still quite warm.</li>
</ul>



<p><strong>RELATED: <a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/strawberry-milk-tea/">Strawberry Bubble Tea</a></strong></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="ingredient-notes">Ingredient Notes</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201200%201800'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Bubble Tea or Boba Milk Tea ingredients on a table in measuring bowls and cups with labels.
" class="wp-image-27036" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1.jpg 1200w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-150x225.jpg 150w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-lazy-src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1.jpg" alt="Bubble Tea or Boba Milk Tea ingredients on a table in measuring bowls and cups with labels.
" class="wp-image-27036" srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1.jpg 1200w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-1-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></noscript></figure>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://collabs.shop/lyawgy" data-eafl-id="19573" data-eafl-parsed="1" class="eafl-link eafl-link-text eafl-link-direct" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored"><strong>Black tea:</strong></a> Any black tea can be used. Tea doesn&rsquo;t need to be the highest quality, so you can use tea bags.</li>



<li><a href="https://amzn.to/2w9MMam" data-eafl-id="18399" data-eafl-parsed="1" class="eafl-link eafl-link-text eafl-link-direct" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored"><strong>Tapioca balls:</strong></a> Store-bought boba only requires them to be boiled in water for a few minutes. It&rsquo;s the quickest and easiest way to make boba at home.</li>



<li><strong>Brown sugar:</strong> Brown sugar gives the drink a deep, rich flavor, but you can use regular white sugar if that&rsquo;s what you have.</li>



<li><strong>Milk:</strong> Any kind of milk can be used but it&rsquo;s especially creamy with whole milk or half &amp; half.</li>



<li><strong>Water:</strong> Tea always tastes better when made with filtered water. </li>



<li><strong>Ice:</strong> Use filtered water if possible to make ice.</li>
</ul>



<p><em>For full ingredients and detailed instructions, please see the recipe card at the bottom of the post.</em></p>


