<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="step-by-step-instructions">Step-by-Step Instructions</h2>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-28f84493 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20730%201095'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="" class="wp-image-29320" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4.jpg 1200w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" data-lazy-src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-730x1095.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-730x1095.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-29320" srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/hojicha-bubble-tea-4.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" /></noscript></figure>



<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Steep tea in hot water. Strain tea leaves or remove tea bag. Stir in brown sugar. Set aside to cool.</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20730%201095'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="" class="wp-image-32894" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5.jpg 1200w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" data-lazy-src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-730x1095.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-730x1095.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-32894" srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/chai-bubble-tea-5.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" /></noscript></figure>



<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Cook tapioca balls in brown sugar and water.</p>
</div>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-28f84493 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20730%201095'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="" class="wp-image-27043" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8.jpg 1200w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" data-lazy-src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-730x1095.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-730x1095.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-27043" srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-8.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" /></noscript></figure>



<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Put tapioca balls into a glass. Add ice and pour in tea.</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20730%201095'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="" class="wp-image-27045" data-lazy-srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10.jpg 1200w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" data-lazy-src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-730x1095.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="730" height="1095" src="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-730x1095.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-27045" srcset="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-730x1095.jpg 730w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-400x600.jpg 400w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-100x150.jpg 100w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/wp-content/uploads/bubble-tea-boba-10.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px" /></noscript></figure>



<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Top with milk. Serve immediately. Stir before drinking. Use an&nbsp;<a href="https://amzn.to/2YDYlTC" data-eafl-id="18400" data-eafl-parsed="1" class="eafl-link eafl-link-text eafl-link-direct" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored"><strong>extra wide straw</strong></a>&nbsp;to drink.</p>
</div>
</div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="recipe-notes">Recipe Notes</h2>



<p><strong>Tapioca balls should be quite warm, but not too hot.</strong><br>To keep the boba soft and chewy, add warm tapioca balls into the drink. The ice will cool it down a bit but make sure you don&rsquo;t use piping hot tapioca balls that can burn your mouth.</p>



<p><strong>Adjust sugar with simple syrup if needed.</strong><br>If you like your drink sweeter, add <strong><a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/brown-sugar-syrup/">brown sugar syrup</a></strong> or plain <strong><a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/simple-syrup/">simple syrup.</a></strong> Sugar will just sink to the bottom of the cup.</p>



<p><strong>Any type of tea can be used.</strong><br>Black tea is used in a classic bubble tea, but you can use any kind of tea you like. Try making bubble tea with green, white, or oolong tea instead of black tea.</p>



<p><strong>RELATED: <a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/oolong-bubble-tea/">Oolong Bubble Tea</a></strong></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="expert-tips">Expert Tips</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Unfortunately, tapioca balls need to be made within just a couple of hours of serving them. They can&rsquo;t be made the day before since they&rsquo;ll harden.</li>



<li>Tea bags contains the lowest quality tea, but since it&rsquo;s going into a drink with sugar and milk, you don&rsquo;t need to use the best tea.</li>



<li>The tea can be made ahead of time and stored in the refrigerator for up to 4 days. Don&rsquo;t add the milk until you&rsquo;re ready to serve the drink.</li>
</ul>



<p><strong>RELATED: <a href="https://www.ohhowcivilized.com/hong-kong-bubble-tea/">Hong Kong Bubble Tea</a></strong></p>



