	<div id="recipe-27236-ingredients" class="wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-ingredients-no-images wprm-recipe-27236-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before" data-recipe="27236" data-servings="1"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-none wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none wprm-header-has-actions" style="">Ingredients&nbsp;<div class="wprm-recipe-adjustable-servings-container wprm-recipe-adjustable-servings-27236-container wprm-toggle-container wprm-toggle-buttons-container wprm-block-text-normal" style="--wprm-toggle-button-background: var(--wp--preset--color--background);--wprm-toggle-button-accent: var(--wp--preset--color--primary);--wprm-toggle-button-radius: 0px;"><button class="wprm-recipe-adjustable-servings wprm-toggle wprm-toggle-active" data-multiplier="1" data-servings="1" data-recipe="27236" aria-label="Adjust servings by 1x">1x</button><button class="wprm-recipe-adjustable-servings wprm-toggle" data-multiplier="2" data-servings="1" data-recipe="27236" aria-label="Adjust servings by 2x">2x</button><button class="wprm-recipe-adjustable-servings wprm-toggle" data-multiplier="3" data-servings="1" data-recipe="27236" aria-label="Adjust servings by 3x">3x</button></div></h3><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-none">Milk Tea</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: none;" data-uid="1"><span class="wprm-checkbox-container"><input type="checkbox" id="wprm-checkbox-0" class="wprm-checkbox" aria-label="&nbsp;1 tablespoon black tea, (or 2 tea bags)"><label for="wprm-checkbox-0" class="wprm-checkbox-label"><span class="sr-only screen-reader-text wprm-screen-reader-text">&#9634; </span></label></span><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name"><a href="https://collabs.shop/lyawgy" class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">black tea</a></span>, <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">(or 2 tea bags)</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: none;" data-uid="0"><span class="wprm-checkbox-container"><input type="checkbox" id="wprm-checkbox-1" class="wprm-checkbox" aria-label="&nbsp;1 cup water"><label for="wprm-checkbox-1" class="wprm-checkbox-label"><span class="sr-only screen-reader-text wprm-screen-reader-text">&#9634; </span></label></span><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">water</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: none;" data-uid="7"><span class="wprm-checkbox-container"><input type="checkbox" id="wprm-checkbox-2" class="wprm-checkbox" aria-label="&nbsp;1 tablespoon brown sugar"><label for="wprm-checkbox-2" class="wprm-checkbox-label"><span class="sr-only screen-reader-text wprm-screen-reader-text">&#9634; </span></label></span><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">brown sugar</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: none;" data-uid="8"><span class="wprm-checkbox-container"><input type="checkbox" id="wprm-checkbox-3" class="wprm-checkbox" aria-label="&nbsp;&frac14; cup milk"><label for="wprm-checkbox-3" class="wprm-checkbox-label"><span class="sr-only screen-reader-text wprm-screen-reader-text">&#9634; </span></label></span><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">milk</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-none">Tapioca Balls</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: none;" data-uid="4"><span class="wprm-checkbox-container"><input type="checkbox" id="wprm-checkbox-4" class="wprm-checkbox" aria-label="&nbsp;&frac34; cup water"><label for="wprm-checkbox-4" class="wprm-checkbox-label"><span class="sr-only screen-reader-text wprm-screen-reader-text">&#9634; </span></label></span><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac34;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">water</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: none;" data-uid="6"><span class="wprm-checkbox-container"><input type="checkbox" id="wprm-checkbox-5" class="wprm-checkbox" aria-label="&nbsp;&frac14; cup tapioca balls"><label for="wprm-checkbox-5" class="wprm-checkbox-label"><span class="sr-only screen-reader-text wprm-screen-reader-text">&#9634; </span></label></span><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name"><a href="https://amzn.to/2w9MMam" class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">tapioca balls</a></span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: none;" data-uid="5"><span class="wprm-checkbox-container"><input type="checkbox" id="wprm-checkbox-6" class="wprm-checkbox" aria-label="&nbsp;2 tablespoons brown sugar"><label for="wprm-checkbox-6" class="wprm-checkbox-label"><span class="sr-only screen-reader-text wprm-screen-reader-text">&#9634; </span></label></span><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">brown sugar</span></li></ul></div></div>
	<div id="recipe-27236-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-27236-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="27236"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-none wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none wprm-header-has-actions" style="">Instructions&nbsp;</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-27236-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text"><span style="display: block;"><strong>Make tea. Steep tea in hot water for 5 minutes.</strong></span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div><span style="display: block;">Set the water temperature to 195&deg;F if you're using an <a href="https://amzn.to/2p03AgN" data-eafl-id="16658" data-eafl-parsed="1" class="eafl-link eafl-link-text eafl-link-direct" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored"><strong>electric kettle with a temperature setting.</strong></a> Use filtered water when possible.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-27236-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text"><span style="display: block;"><strong>Strain tea leaves. Stir in brown sugar. </strong></span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div><span style="display: block;">Set aside to cool.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-27236-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text"><span style="display: block;"><strong>Cook tapioca balls. Boil &frac34; cup of water and sugar in a saucepan. Add tapioca balls.</strong></span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div><span style="display: block;">Combine brown sugar and &frac34; cup of water in a saucepan and bring it to a boil. When you see big bubbles (2-4 minutes), add tapioca balls. Keep boiling for 8 more minutes on medium-high heat. Cool slightly, until tapioca balls aren't too hot to eat. They should still be quite warm.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-27236-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text"><span style="display: block;"><strong>Assemble the drink. Add warm tapioca balls in brown sugar syrup into a cup. Add ice, tea, and milk.</strong></span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div><span style="display: block;">Serve immediately and stir before drinking. Use an&nbsp;<a href="https://amzn.to/2YDYlTC" data-eafl-id="18400" data-eafl-parsed="1" class="eafl-link eafl-link-text eafl-link-direct" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored"><strong>extra wide straw</strong></a>&nbsp;to drink.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>
	<div id="recipe-video"></div>
	<div id="recipe-27236-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-none wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li>Brown sugar gives the drink a deep, rich flavor, but you can use regular white sugar if that&rsquo;s what you have.</li>
<li>Any kind of milk can be used but it&rsquo;s especially creamy with whole milk or half &amp; half.</li>
<li>Black tea is used in a classic bubble tea, but you can use any kind of tea you like.</li>
<li>To keep the boba soft and chewy, add warm tapioca balls into the drink. The ice will cool it down a bit but make sure you don&rsquo;t use piping hot tapioca balls that can burn your mouth.</li>
<li>Unfortunately, tapioca balls need to be made within just a couple of hours of serving them. They can&rsquo;t be made the day before since they&rsquo;ll harden.</li>
<li>The tea can be made ahead of time and stored in the refrigerator for up to 4 days. Don&rsquo;t add the milk until you&rsquo;re ready to serve the drink.</li>
</ul></div></div>
	<div class="cwp-food-nutrition">
